/* =========================================================================
   COURSE CATALOG for the Course Planner (and any page that needs the full course list).
   Source: Archbishop Moeller Curriculum Guide 2026-2027 plus the counselors' course worksheet.
   The guide is the authority; where the worksheet disagreed, the guide won (see the hand-off notes).

   HOW TO UPDATE EACH YEAR (when the new Curriculum Guide comes out):
     1. Walk each department section of the guide (The Arts, Business and Applied Technologies, English,
        Mathematics, Physical Education, Religion, Science, Social Studies, Student Support, World Languages).
        For every course heading check: title, level, grades in parentheses, "semester"/"year", prerequisites,
        corequisites, and sentences such as "does not meet graduation requirements for ..." (the counts field).
     2. Add new courses as a new { ... } line. Remove courses that are gone. Keep ids the same from year to year
        (saved student plans refer to ids), so if a course is renamed keep its old id and change only the title.
     3. Update the page numbers (page: n). Pages are the guide's printed page numbers.
     4. Check the Course List pages (pp.13-14) for level codes: "Classes are CP1 unless noted".
     5. Run the check described at the bottom of this file (node) before publishing.

   FIELD MEANINGS (every entry has every field; empty means "" or []):
     id         stable slug, unique. Never reuse an id for a different course.
     title      course name exactly as a student would see it in the guide (level suffix included).
     dept       one of: Religion, English, Mathematics, Science, Social Studies, World Languages, Fine Arts,
                Business & Technology, Health & PE, Student Support, Other.
     alsoDepts  other department sections that also list this course (informational).
     level      CP2 | CP1 Level 1 | CP1 | Honors | Honors+ | AP | CCP | PF (pass/fail) | "" (no level given).
     credits    0.25 | 0.5 | 1 | 1.5 (Band earns 1.5). CCP semester courses earn 1 credit (worksheet).
     term       year | semester | summer. "online" is shown with the online flag instead, so the length stays known.
     online     true when the guide says the course is online (no scheduled meeting time).
     grades     grade levels that may take it, e.g. [9] or [10,11,12].
     prereq     ids of courses that must ALL be completed first (hard prerequisites named in the guide).
     prereqAny  list of groups; ONE course from EACH group must be completed first, e.g. [["bio-cp1","bio-h"]].
     prereqNote the guide's own wording when it names a grade threshold, placement exam, approval, etc.
     recommended ids the guide lists as "recommended prerequisite" (advice, not a block).
     coreq      ids that must be taken at the same time (or earlier). coreqAny works like prereqAny.
     counts     which graduation requirement the course satisfies: Religion | English | Mathematics | Science |
                Social Studies | World Language | Fine Arts | Financial Literacy | Health | Oral Communications |
                Physical Education | Electives | MoeTerm | None.
                "Electives" = counts only toward the 2 elective credits (the guide says it does not meet the
                department's requirement, or it is an elective by nature). "None" = counts toward nothing.
     countsNote the guide's sentence behind an unusual counts value.
     language   French | German | Latin | Spanish | ASL (world language courses only).
     sciTag     Biology | Chemistry | Physics | Earth Science (used by the science rule).
     ssTag      US History | World History | Government (used by the social studies rule).
     bundle     for the freshman arts pairings only: the two semester courses the option is made of.
     page       the guide page where the course is described.
     source     both (worksheet and guide) | guide (guide only) | worksheet (worksheet only; not in this guide).
     note       anything a counselor should know (aliases, conflicts between sources, special credit).

   VALIDATION (run from the site folder):
     node -e "global.window={};require('./assets/data/course-catalog.js');require('./assets/data/course-rules.js');"
     The team check script also verifies unique ids, that every prereq/coreq id exists, and allowed values.
   ========================================================================= */

